      "writtenOn": "2026-02-19T22:23:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Immutability and persistence are two orthogonal properties,\n\nIn general, yes. But for the case of Gerrit\u0027s persisted caches, I think they\u0027re always immutable.\n\n\u003e I don\u0027t see any coupling here between these two properties. Forwarding cache evictions between primaries is a mean to remove stale entries from cache on other primaries.\n\nTo my point above, I don\u0027t think you ever need to forward an eviction for a persisted cache. Evictions for persisted caches are effectively based on size constraints, not staleness.",
      "parentUuid": "ebcdec4d_0427438d",
      "revId": "cc0158e20c2db5080e51e0439c39cfccf2814314",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5274a4f_78212fcd",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
